# CKA Lab Exercise: Kubernetes Networking (Services, Ingress, Gateway API & Network Policies)

Hands-on training scenario for the Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) certification, covering Services, Ingress controllers, the Gateway API (with NGINX Gateway Fabric & Caddy reverse proxy), and Network Policies (tested with httpbin-go).

---

## 1. Overview & Curriculum Objectives

Networking constitutes a major domain of the CKA exam curriculum. This lab brings together the core networking primitives and modern architectural patterns:

- **Module 1 (Services & CoreDNS)**: Stable ClusterIP networking, DNS resolution (`<service>.<namespace>.svc.cluster.local`), multi-port NodePort services, and modern endpoint / EndpointSlice mapping.
- **Module 2 (Ingresses)**: L7 HTTP/HTTPS traffic routing via standard Ingress resources, host-based routing, and path-prefix matching.
- **Module 3 (Gateway API)**: Next-generation role-oriented routing using standard Gateway API CRDs (`GatewayClass`, `Gateway`, `HTTPRoute`), NGINX Gateway Fabric, and Caddy TLS edge forwarding.
- **Module 4 (Network Policies)**: Microsegmentation, default-deny ingress/egress, pod and namespace label selectors, DNS port 53 allow rules, and verification via `httpbin-go`.

